  "review": {
    "book": "2SA",
    "entityID": "person:abishai_50",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "The three sons of Zeruiah were there: Joab, Abishai, and Asahel. Asahel was as light of foot as a wild gazelle."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Joab and Abishai pursued Abner. The sun went down when they had come to the hill of Ammah, that lies before Giah by the way of the wilderness of Gibeon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Joab and Abishai his brother killed Abner, because he had killed their brother Asahel at Gibeon in the battle."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA10:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "The rest of the people he committed into the hand of Abishai his brother; and he put them in array against the children of Ammon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA10:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians had fled, they likewise fled before Abishai, and entered into the city. Then Joab returned from the children of Ammon and came to Jerusalem."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Abishai the son of Zeruiah said to the king, “Why should this dead dog curse my lord the king? Please let me go over and take off his head.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said to Abishai and to all his servants, “Behold, my son, who came out of my bowels, seeks my life. How much more this Benjamite, now? Leave him alone, and let him curse; for the LORD has invited him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA18:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "David sent the people out, a third part under the hand of Joab, and a third part under the hand of Abishai the son of Zeruiah, Joab’s brother, and a third part under the hand of Ittai the Gittite. The king said to the people, “I will also surely go out with you myself.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA18:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king commanded Joab and Abishai and Ittai, saying, “Deal gently for my sake with the young man Absalom.” All the people heard when the king commanded all the captains concerning Absalom."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA18:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "The man said to Joab, “Though I should receive a thousand pieces of silver in my hand, I still wouldn’t stretch out my hand against the king’s son; for in our hearing the king commanded you and Abishai and Ittai, saying, ‘Beware that no one touch the young man Absalom.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA19:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Abishai the son of Zeruiah answered, “Shouldn’t Shimei be put to death for this, because he cursed the LORD’s anointed?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA20:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said to Abishai, “Now Sheba the son of Bichri will do us more harm than Absalom did. Take your lord’s servants and pursue after him, lest he get himself fortified cities, and escape out of our sight.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA20:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Amasa took no heed to the sword that was in Joab’s hand. So he struck him with it in the body and shed out his bowels to the ground, and didn’t strike him again; and he died. Joab and Abishai his brother pursued Sheba the son of Bichri."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA21:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Abishai the son of Zeruiah helped him, and struck the Philistine and killed him. Then the men of David swore to him, saying, “Don’t go out with us to battle any more, so that you don’t quench the lamp of Israel.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA23:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abishai, the brother of Joab, the son of Zeruiah, was chief of the three. He lifted up his spear against three hundred and killed them, and had a name among the three."
      }
    ],
